1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,950
“…the aggressive impulses of an evil empire.”

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,340
September, 1983.

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:08,250
The Cold War is at its most dangerous.

4
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:11,600
Thousands of nuclear missiles stand ready to fly.

5
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,620
Just after midnight,

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,810
in a secret bunker outside Moscow,

7
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:18,620
Lieutenant Colonel Stanislav Petrov is on duty.

8
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:20,860
Then, the alarm.

9
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,950
Satellites report an American missile launch.

10
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:25,440
Then another.

11
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,150
Five in all.

12
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,970
Protocol says: report it.

13
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:33,270
A Soviet counterstrike could follow within minutes.

14
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:35,600
But Petrov doubts it.

15
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,640
A real first strike would mean hundreds of missiles,

16
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:39,730
not five.

17
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:42,310
Ground radar confirms nothing.

18
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,850
He calls it a false alarm.

19
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,710
He was right.

20
00:00:47,210 --> 00:00:50,070
Sunlight on high clouds had fooled the satellites.

21
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:52,690
Petrov received no medal.

22
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:55,970
His story stayed secret for fifteen years.

23
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:00,000
The man who saved the world.

